## EXPERIMENTAL SECTION
Materials and Reagents. Iron (Ⅲ) chloride hexahydrate $(\mathrm{FeCl}_{3}{\bullet}6\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O})$ and terephthalic acid $(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{BDC})$ (Aladdin, Shanghai, China) were used to prepare MIL-101 (Fe). 2, 2’- azino-bis-(3- ethylbenzthiazoline-6-sulfonic acid) diammonium salt (ABTS), tannic acid (TA), $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}$ and $\mathrm{AgNO}_{3}$ were obtained from Aladdin. Crystal violet (CV), rhodamine 6G (Rh 6G), malachite green (MG) and $p$ -aminothiophenol $(p\cdot$ ATP) were purchased from Beijing Dingguo Biological Technology Co., Ltd. All reagents were analytical grade and commercial, and used without further purification. All solutions were prepared using ultra-pure water $\cdot18.2\ensuremath{\mathrm{M}}\Omega)$ .
Fabrication of SERS-Active AgNPs/MIL-101 (Fe) Hybrid. MIL-101 (Fe) was synthesized according to previous report.28 The anchored Ag NPs were prepared via in situ synthesis strategy by utilizing TA as a reductant. Typically, $15~\mathrm{mg}$ of activated MIL-101 was suspended in $9.5~\mathrm{mL}$ $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{\cdot}$ , and then $0.5~\mathrm{mL}$ TA solution $20~\mathrm{mg}$ TA dissolved in 0.5 mL $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ ) was rapidly injected into the mixture under vigorous stirring. For further stirring of $20~\mathrm{s}$ , the mazarine products (TA/MIL-101) isolated by centrifugation and washed with $_\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ for three times to remove the excess TA. Then, TA/MIL-101 was redispersed in $9.5~\mathrm{mL}$ $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ , then $0.5{\bf M}$ ${\mathrm{K}}_{2}{\mathrm{CO}}_{3}$ was used to tune $\mathsf{p H}$ of the suspension to 7.5. Finally, $0.5~\mathrm{mL}$ $\mathrm{AgNO}_{3}$ (0.05 M, 0.1 M, $0.15{\mathrm{M}}$ and $0.2{\bf M}$ , respectively) was added dropwise under a stirring speed of $600~\mathrm{rpm}$ at room temperature. After further stirring for $^\textrm{\scriptsize1h}$ , the dark products (AgNPs/MIL-101) was isolated by centrifugation and washed with $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ three times, and the obtained AgNPs/MIL-101 was dried in vacuum freezing drying oven for further use.
SERS Activity of $\mathbf{AgNPs/MIL-101}$ Composite as Substrate. In this SERS study, common SERS model analytes, such as CV, Rh 6G, MG and $p$ -ATP, were performed to characterize the SERS activity of the AgNPs/MIL-101 composite. The Ag NPs about $40\ \mathrm{nm}$ and the bare MIL-101 were used as controls. Typically, ${5\upmu\mathrm{L}}$ Ag NPs, MIL-101 and AgNPs/MIL101 solution $\mathrm{1~mg/mL}$ , respectively) mixed with $95~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ SERS model analytes and incubated for 30 minutes at the room temperature, and then the mixtures were used for SERS detection (Figure S4, SI). Parameter setting: Laser wavelength, $532\mathrm{nm}$ ; power, $28\mathrm{mW}$ ; lens, $50\times$ objective; acquisition time, $10~\mathrm{s}$ .
Detection of DA in Aqueous Medium and Urine. DA analysis was carried out as follows: $10~{\upmu\mathrm{L}}~0.2~\mathrm{M}$ NaAc buffer solution $\mathrm{(pH~4.0)}$ , $10~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ $\mathrm{AgNPs/MIL-}101$ aqueous solution $\left(1.0\mathrm{\mg/mL}\right)$ , $10~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ 1.0 mM $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}$ , and $10~{\upmu\mathrm{L}}~10~\mathrm{mM}$ ABTS were added into $200~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ EP vial. Then, a certain amount of DA or urine was added into the above reaction solution. The resultant mixture was incubated at $40~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $20~\mathrm{min}$ and then used for DA measurement by monitoring the Raman shifts at
